      "text": "Arbitrary Call over flash() Vulnerable code snippet: https://arbiscan.io/address/0x598c6c1cd9459f882530fc9d7da438cb74c6cb3b Attack tx: https://arbiscan.io/tx/0x5d2a94785d95a740ec5f778e79ff014c880bcefec70d1a7c2440e611f84713d6 https://app.blocksec.com/explorer/tx/arbitrum/0x5d2a94785d95a740ec5f778e79ff014c880bcefec70d1a7c2440e611f84713d6 Analysis: https://x.com/ricocreditsys/status/1781803698940781009 %202b25db69bd4944fca7f82fb0edff98f1/Screenshot_2024-07-04_at_1.50.27_PM.png)"
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "Rico on Arbitrum One was exploited on April 20, 2024, due to unchecked arbitrary external calls in a privileged flash loan function. The attacker drained approximately $36,000 from the protocol by commanding asset transfers to themselves and swapping the proceeds to USDC. The BankDiamond contract's flash loan function allowed arbitrary external call execution without restricting caller permissions or validating call targets, letting the attacker transfer protocol assets directly."
    }
